---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Scribble from "@/components/Scribble.astro";

const title = "About the Vibe Coding Drift";
const description = "Notes from a castaway drifting through the vast AI ocean.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="app-layout py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <div class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.4em] text-accent-dim uppercase mb-6 font-bold">THE DRIFT</div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-serif italic text-ink tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-8">
          Notes from the <Scribble type="underline">AI Ocean.</Scribble>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary font-serif italic leading-relaxed">
          "I don't have a roadmap. I have a terminal and a current. I'm just here to see what the tide brings in."
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-ink max-w-none font-serif text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          The AI world is a vast, chaotic ocean. Every day a new paper drops, a new model ships, a new open-source library changes the game. 
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm not an architect building a skyscraper. I'm a <Scribble type="circle">Castaway</Scribble> drifting through the waves. I spend my days messing with agents, testing weird prompts, and trying to make sense of the "vibe."
        </p>
        
        <div class="my-16 p-8 border-l-4 border-accent bg-accent/5 italic">
          "The goal isn't to reach a destination. It's to learn the currents."
        </div>

        
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif italic text-ink mt-12 mb-6">Studying the Gurus</h3>
        <p>
          I don't drift blindly. I follow the beacons lit by the true masters. 
        </p>
        <p>
          I spend hours deconstructing <strong>Andrej Karpathy's</strong> insights on LLM mental models, mapping the "vibe coding" philosophy he defined. I obsess over the technical clarity of <strong>Dan Abramov</strong> and the pragmatic engineering of <strong>Kent C. Dodds</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          This isn't just about using AI; it's about <Scribble type="circle">apprenticeship</Scribble> in the age of intelligence. I am a student of their rigor, trying to apply their deep-thinking patterns to my chaotic drift.
        </p>

<h3 class="text-3xl font-serif italic text-ink mt-12 mb-6">The Accidental Engine: MUSU</h3>
        <p>
          Along the way, I realized I needed a better way to survive. I had too many machines, too much slop, and not enough control. 
        </p>
        <p>
          So, I started forging <Scribble type="underline">MUSU</Scribble>—the engine that helps me manage the drift. It's the raft I'm building while I explore the open-source islands. You'll see it pop up in the logs as it evolves from a script into a service.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif italic text-ink mt-12 mb-6">What I'm tracking</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Tide Reports:</strong> Deep dives into new AI tools and open-source projects.</li>
          <li><strong>Vibe Logs:</strong> The raw, unpolished reality of trying to make AI do what I actually mean.</li>
          <li><strong>The Forging of MUSU:</strong> How the need for order in the drift led to a real product.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-20">
          <a href="/posts" class="bg-ink text-background px-8 py-4 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-black hover:bg-ink/90 transition-colors inline-block">
            View the Field Logs
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
